# Scraped corpus + HTTP cache (unlicensed source data, keep local)
data_pipeline/cache/
data_pipeline/out/

# NOTE: backend/idoma_dictionary_v3.json used to be ignored here, to avoid
# republishing 1,117 idomaland.org pairs as a bulk download from a public repo.
# It is committed now because it is no longer that file: it is 226 curated,
# tone-marked entries (the previous v3 merged with idoma_dictionary.json by
# data_pipeline/merge_dictionary.py), not the scraped corpus. The corpus itself
# stays unpublished under data_pipeline/out/ above.
#
# Keeping it ignored had a real cost: Render builds from git, so every deploy
# silently fell back to the fabricated v2 and served "òhụ" for house while the
# model answered words the dictionary was supposed to cover.
#
# If you regenerate the full 1,117-entry corpus dictionary with
# data_pipeline/build_dictionary.py, restore this line before committing.

# TypeScript build artifacts
tsconfig.*.tsbuildinfo
